Sat Aug 22 08:05:18 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 2.68.1:
  * Update the inlined @picsart/ai-sdk to 5.x so edit, enhance,
    upscale, TTS and related flows match the new catalog (they
    selected no models after the SDK 5 shape change) and hide
    deprecated models
  * Fix a crash after generation when xdg-open is missing, Ctrl+C
    cancel handling, prompt-box corruption, wide-character widths
    and ANSI sequences leaking into piped stdout
  * Harden login and token refresh (timeouts, atomic writes, CI
    PICSART_ACCESS_TOKEN, 401 retry) and reject directory uploads
  * Sanitize untrusted API and model names so they cannot inject
    terminal escape sequences
  * Wire video-extend array file slots, keep edit-mode parameters
    and expand ~ in downloadDir
  * Honour config defaultModel and imagePreview

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 13 11:15:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Rename the package from gen-ai to picsart-gen-ai, following a
  review comment on the Factory submission: the tool is a client for
  one specific hosted service and should not hold the generic name
  * The installed command stays /usr/bin/gen-ai, which is what
    upstream's documentation and npx invocations use; only the RPM
    name is qualified with the service
  * Obsolete gen-ai up to 2.60.1, the only version it ever shipped, so
    a copy installed from the devel project is replaced instead of
    co-installed; the bound is frozen rather than tracking the version,
    and the generic name is deliberately not provided back, since
    either would keep laying claim to a name this rename gives up
  * Introduce an npm_name macro for the upstream tarball, the nodejs
    module directory and the command, all of which keep the upstream
    name now that the package name differs from it

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Aug 10 18:03:30 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package (version 2.60.1):
  * Command line client for Picsart's generative AI service, which
    creates and edits images, video and audio from the terminal
  * Interactive picker for models and their parameters, batch re-runs
    of failed jobs and a browsable history of past generations
  * Requires a Picsart account; nothing is generated locally
- Package the published npm bundle rather than the git tree: upstream
  inlines two dependencies from a private registry that cannot be
  resolved downstream, so the git tree does not build outside Picsart
- Vendor the runtime dependencies with the node_modules OBS service:
  package-lock.json is the input, node_modules.obscpio the offline
  tarball set consumed by local-npm-registry at build time
